<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="authority" xml:lang="eng">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Kanchi authority file: places, deities and monuments</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <publisher>Unpublished demonstration repository</publisher>
        <availability status="free">
          <licence target="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">
            <p>CC BY 4.0.</p>
          </licence>
        </availability>
        <date when="2026-09-20"/>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>External identifiers were resolved against Wikidata and verified on
        2026-09-20. Coordinates are taken from Wikidata P625.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
    <encodingDesc>
      <editorialDecl>
        <p>Every entity carries a project-local URI. External alignment is recorded in
        <gi>idno</gi> elements typed by authority. Where no external record exists the
        entity is still given a project URI and the gap is stated explicitly rather
        than silently omitted, so that alignment coverage can be measured.</p>
      </editorialDecl>
    </encodingDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="places">
        <listPlace>
          <place xml:id="place-madurai" type="settlement">
            <placeName xml:lang="eng">Madurai</placeName>
            <placeName xml:lang="tam">மதுரை</placeName>
            <placeName xml:lang="san-Latn">Madhurā</placeName>
            <location>
              <geo decls="#WGS84">9.925201 78.119775</geo>
            </location>
            <idno type="wikidata">http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q228405</idno>
            <idno type="gnd">https://d-nb.info/gnd/4275927-4</idno>
            <idno type="geonames">https://sws.geonames.org/1264521/</idno>
            <note xml:lang="eng">The temple city whose legends this corpus
            transmits.</note>
          </place>
        </listPlace>
      </div>
      <div type="monuments">
        <listPlace>
          <place xml:id="monument-meenakshi-temple" type="temple">
            <placeName xml:lang="eng">Meenakshi Amman Temple</placeName>
            <placeName xml:lang="tam">மீனாட்சி அம்மன் கோயில்</placeName>
            <idno type="wikidata">http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1424358</idno>
          </place>
        </listPlace>
      </div>
      <div type="deities">
        <listPerson>
          <person xml:id="deity-shiva" role="deity">
            <persName xml:lang="eng">Shiva</persName>
            <persName xml:lang="san">शिव</persName>
            <persName xml:lang="tam">சிவன்</persName>
            <idno type="wikidata">http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11378</idno>
            <idno type="gnd">https://d-nb.info/gnd/118755218</idno>
            <note xml:lang="eng">At Madurai, Shiva is worshipped under the local
            epithet Sundareshvara/Sundareswarar. This is not a separate deity and is
            deliberately not given its own authority entity or <att>owl:sameAs</att>
            link — see docs/adr/0005.</note>
          </person>
          <person xml:id="deity-meenakshi" role="deity">
            <persName xml:lang="eng">Meenakshi</persName>
            <persName xml:lang="san">मीनाक्षी</persName>
            <persName xml:lang="tam">மீனாட்சி</persName>
            <idno type="wikidata">http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1520192</idno>
          </person>
        </listPerson>
      </div>
      <div type="languages">
        <list>
          <item xml:id="lang-san">Sanskrit
            <idno type="wikidata">http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11059</idno>
          </item>
          <item xml:id="lang-tam">Tamil
            <idno type="wikidata">http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5885</idno>
          </item>
        </list>
      </div>
      <div type="section">
        <listRelation type="cultic">
          <relation name="located-in" active="#monument-meenakshi-temple"
                    passive="#place-madurai"/>
          <!-- Deliberately "worshipped-at" rather than owl:sameAs: the goddess and
               the building are distinct resources. See docs/adr/0005. -->
          <relation name="worshipped-at" active="#deity-meenakshi"
                    passive="#monument-meenakshi-temple"/>
          <relation name="worshipped-at" active="#deity-shiva"
                    passive="#place-madurai"/>
        </listRelation>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
</TEI>
